# SDLC ecosystem (PersonaLearn)

## Platform roles

| System | Owns |
|--------|------|
| **Jira (PSL)** | Tickets, sprint, status, blockers |
| **Confluence (PLEARN)** | Specs, ADRs, release notes, retros |
| **GitHub** | Code, branches, PRs, CI, release tags |
| **Slack (#personalearn-dev)** | Notifications only — not source of truth |

Notion is **out of the official traceability chain**. Do not create SDLC artifacts there.

**Confluence hub:** https://nervustechnologies.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLEARN/overview

## Golden thread

Every unit of work traces to `PSL-N` via mandatory GitHub Issue intake:

```
GitHub Issue → Jira ticket (PSL-N) → Confluence spec → GitHub branch/PR → Slack notification
```

A **GitHub Issue is REQUIRED** for every feature and bug **before** a Jira `PSL-N` is created, a branch is opened, or implementation begins. The Issue carries `needs-triage` + best-guess `type-*`, an **assignee**, and a **milestone** until mirrored to `PSL-N` with `area-*` + `type-*` copied across.

If work does not link to a GitHub Issue and `PSL-N`, treat it as unofficial until triaged.

## Jira workflow (PSL)

| Status | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **To Do** | Backlog; spec linked before sprint pull |
| **In Progress** | Branch exists; active implementation |
| **Review** | PR open; CI/review in flight |
| **Blocker** | Blocked on dependency or external factor |
| **Done** | Merged to `develop` |

Complements `git-workflow.mdc`. For step-by-step delivery (branch → PR → review → merge), use the **`sdlc-pr-lifecycle`** skill.

## Labels & tagging (Jira + GitHub)

Labels, assignee, and sprint metadata are required on **every** tracked item. Use the same `area-*` / `type-*` vocabulary on Jira tickets, GitHub Issues, and GitHub PRs.

**Area (exactly one):** `area-auth`, `area-dashboard`, `area-classes`, `area-ai-rag`, `area-infra`, `area-docs`

**Type (exactly one):** `type-feature`, `type-bug`, `type-chore`, `type-tech-debt`

Do **not** use GitHub’s default `bug` / `enhancement` labels — use `type-bug` / `type-feature`.

**GitHub Issue intake (mandatory):** Every feature and bug **must** start as a GitHub Issue with `needs-triage` + best-guess `type-*` (and best-guess `area-*` when known). Assign **`nervustech`** (or the owner if different). Set milestone to the **current sprint**, or **Backlog** if unscheduled. A Jira `PSL-N` is created only after that Issue exists; labels + assignee are copied to the ticket and the Issue is linked. Remove `needs-triage` when triaged. No branch or implementation without Issue → `PSL-N`.

**Sprint:** Jira **Sprint** field (primary). GitHub Issue **and** PR **milestone** = current sprint when in an active sprint; otherwise `Backlog`.

**Default GitHub assignee:** `nervustech` whenever the item has no assignee.

**PR reviewer:** Request a reviewer **other than the author** when a second collaborator exists. Solo-dev: skip the request (GitHub blocks self-review); post a review **comment** with verdict per `sdlc-pr-lifecycle`.

Reference vocabulary: Jira PSL-35 (do not delete).

### When labels and fields are required

| Artifact | When | Required |
|----------|------|----------|
| **GitHub Issue** | On create (**mandatory**, precedes Jira) | `needs-triage` + best-guess `type-*` (+ `area-*` when known); **assignee**; **milestone** (sprint or Backlog) |
| **Jira ticket** | On create or triage (only after Issue exists) | `area-*` + `type-*` before leaving To Do; **assignee**; link Issue |
| **GitHub PR** | On open / before review | Same `area-*` + `type-*` as `PSL-N`; **assignee**; **sprint milestone**; **reviewer** (or solo-dev review comment); `## Test plan` in body |
| **GitHub PR** | Before Approve / merge | **Test plan boxes checked** (`[x]`). Run the listed steps, then edit the PR body. Leave unchecked only if marked N/A with a reason |
| **GitHub Issue** | When `PSL-N` is **Done** / PR merged | Close with `state_reason=completed`; keep labels + assignee + milestone |
| **Jira ticket** | After PR review | Re-verify; add follow-up ticket with `type-tech-debt` if needed |

Fix missing or wrong labels, assignee, milestone, or reviewer **before** review verdicts or merge. Do **not** Approve or merge while any Test plan item is still `[ ]` unless it is marked N/A with a reason. Do not leave a shipped ticket’s GitHub Issue open.

### Comment tagging

Every cross-system comment must include `PSL-N` and a link where applicable.

| Where | When | Include |
|-------|------|---------|
| **Jira** | Branch / PR open / review / merge | `PSL-N`, branch or PR URL, verdict on review |
| **GitHub PR** | Review | `PSL-N`, verdict, label confirmation, Test plan checked |
| **GitHub Issue** | Triage reply | `PSL-N` link, labels, assignee, milestone |
| **Slack** | PR open / merge | `PSL-N`, PR URL, one-line summary |

Use `@mention` only when someone must act.

## Ticket description template

```markdown
## Ready checklist
- [ ] Confluence spec linked
- [ ] Acceptance criteria defined
- [ ] No open blocker links
- [ ] Area + type labels set
- [ ] Assignee set
- [ ] Sprint (Jira) / milestone (GitHub) set

## Acceptance criteria
- ...

## Spec
Duplicate Product requirements template in PLEARN (Create → Page → template picker)
```

## Confluence

Use native Atlassian blueprints — **duplicate via Create → Page**, do not hand-roll structure:

| Section | Blueprint |
|---------|-----------|
| Specs | Product requirements |
| Architecture | Decision documentation |
| Releases | Status update |
| Retros | Retrospective |

Populate per ticket/sprint, not bulk upfront. Hub: [PLEARN](https://nervustechnologies.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLEARN/overview).

## GitHub

- **Assignee:** `nervustech` on every Issue and PR that has none
- **Milestone:** current sprint on Issues and PRs in that sprint; `Backlog` otherwise
- **Reviewer:** requested on every PR when a non-author collaborator exists
- **Test plan:** PR body `## Test plan` checkboxes must be `[x]` (or N/A + reason) before Approve / merge
- **Release tags:** `v0.x.0` on `main` when promoting `develop` → `main`
- **GitHub Projects:** not used — Jira board is the backlog
- **Close Issues** when the linked `PSL-N` is Done (do not leave intake Issues open after ship)

## Human gates

Agents must stop and ask for:

- Merge approval
- Merge while Test plan items are still unchecked
- Commit (unless user explicitly requests)
- Scope changes beyond ticket ACs
- Creating new Jira tickets without triage (use `triage-issue` skill for bugs)
- Creating a Jira ticket or branch **without a preceding GitHub Issue** (mandatory intake)
